@startuml
' @guidance:
' Create or update the PlantUML diagram describing the Episodes Act processing flow.
' Keep this diagram simple: a short linear flow with minimal partitions,
' one decision point, and explanatory notes instead of nested detail.


title Ghostwriter - Episodes Act Processing

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED

start

:Parse the act command;
note right
  Expands ">" shorthand, defaults blank input to
  "help", separates the act name from its prompt,
  and reads an episode selector such as "#1,3!".
end note

:Load the act definition and configure it;
note right
  Loads built-in and custom TOML, resolves
  "basedOn" inheritance, applies defaults and
  prompt values, and prepares the episode list.
end note

:Find project files to process;
note right
  Module traversal is handled by the shared
  project processor. Parent-project children are
  filtered by match rules and exclusions. If no
  child matches, the project directory is used.
end note

:Process each selected file in turn;

if (Specific episodes were requested?) then (yes)
  :Run the selected episodes in request order;
  if (Continue with normal order?) then (yes)
    :Continue with the next episode;
  else (no)
    :Finish this file;
  endif
else (no)
  :Start with episode 1;
endif

:Run the episode sequence;
note right
  Each episode combines act metadata, process
  information, instructions, and its prompt;
  it resolves episode tools and calls the provider.
  Repeat requests rerun the episode, while move
  requests jump to a numeric or named episode.
end note

:Collect the file result;
note right
  Continue with the next matching file unless an
  episode signals that the task should end. After
  all files complete, the accumulated act results
  are available to the caller.
end note

stop

legend right
  * Episodes are ordered steps within one act.
  * A caller can select specific episodes and choose
    whether normal order continues afterward.
  * Each episode receives act metadata and can repeat,
    jump to another episode, or end task processing.
endlegend
@enduml
